stateDiagram-v2
    %% CURRENT implementation; sources and guards in transition inventory.
    state "pending" as pending
    state "verified" as verified
    state "consumed" as consumed
    state "canceled" as canceled
    state "expired" as expired
    state "revoked" as revoked
    %% expired, canceled and revoked are absorbing terminal states.
    [*] --> pending
    pending --> verified: record_verification! / record_registration_verification!
    verified --> verified: prepare_result_delivery!
    pending --> canceled: Base cancellation committer
    pending --> expired: Base cancellation at TTL
    pending --> revoked: token revoke_step_up_authority!
    verified --> canceled: Base cancellation committer
    verified --> expired: Base cancellation at TTL
    verified --> revoked: token revoke_step_up_authority!
    verified --> consumed: Base freshness / registration final committer
    pending --> consumed: Base registration consumption for email_otp only
    pending --> consumed: consume_email_registration! original locked parent after Source commit
    revoked --> [*]
    consumed --> [*]
    canceled --> [*]
    note right of pending
        Auth proof returns to owning Base operation.
        The single named model writer rejects every terminal rewrite.
        expired is stored only by the owner expiry operation.
        Cancellation, expiry and revocation cannot rewrite a terminal.
        Generic result delivery is not an authorization shortcut.
        consumed registration proof does not grant freshness.
        Base cancellation/freshness require a usable DeviceSession and its current root.
        Base locks owner, device, token, then ceremony parent.
    end note
